        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Does it track belt speed, does it need your
            weight, and which end is it at?</strong> Those three answers separate a
            loose bolt from a bearing from a dry deck. Tighten the hardware first —
            it is the most common cause and the cheapest fix.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Never reach for WD-40; only 100 per cent silicone goes near a deck, per
            the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubrication guide</a>.
            And if the noise is grinding rather than squeaking, and worsening, stop
            using the machine and read the
            <a href="/treadmill-troubleshooting/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">troubleshooting guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
